            <ArticleTitle>Orofacial pain - a presenting symptom of bisphosphonate associated osteonecrosis of the jaws.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>91-2</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Osteonecrosis of the jaws (ONJ) associated with bisphosphonate therapy is being reported with increasing frequency all over the world. Pain may be the presenting symptom commonly associated with intra-oral bone exposure. The aetiology of this therapeutic complication is still not well understood. Three cases are presented and the management of the condition is discussed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
